─── app/static/bag-search.css:1376-1385 ───
[maintainability · medium] Layout mismatch with the container: in `bags.html` this span is a direct
child of `.bag-scene-cell`, which is `display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px`. Sibling
badges (`.bag-scene-badge`, `.bag-scene-history`) use `align-self: flex-start` to stay as compact,
left-aligned pills. Without it, this badge will stretch to the full width of the cell (min 120px),
and `margin-left: 6px` (an inline-flow offset) shifts it 6px right, misaligning it with the other
badges in the column — the column's `gap: 4px` already handles vertical spacing. `display:
inline-block` also has no effect here, since flex items are blockified. Suggested fix: drop
`display` and `margin-left`, add `align-self: flex-start`.



